+
+    /* Vessel: a save that failed must not be published.
+     *
+     * SaveData returns bool and the result was dropped, so the .new file was
+     * renamed into place whatever happened -- which is how a cache that the
+     * loader refuses came to exist at all. The `.new`-then-rename dance is there
+     * to make publication atomic, and it did that faithfully: it atomically
+     * published a file that could not be read.
+     *
+     * Measured on Resident Evil Requiem: every session generated a cache, every
+     * session refused it on load, and the compile time was spent again the next
+     * launch. The refusal is a real one -- see the sibling change in
+     * CodeCache.cpp for why a code buffer swap during generation leaves the
+     * relocation table pointing into a buffer that no longer exists -- and the
